        Explicit width/height attributes match the source resolution
        so the browser allocates the full texture instead of decoding
        at the CSS box size (the var(--hex-w/h) cell sizing) and then
        upscaling via transform: scale() — that's what made the photo
        look pixelated even though the source file is sharp (user
        feedback 2026-05-15: "primární obrázek je rozpixelovaný").
        fetchpriority="high" pushes it ahead of the other grid
        photos so the hero state is sharp on first paint.
      -->
